  mainEntity: [{
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: 'Does the same Traverse WASM give byte-identical output on every host?',
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: 'The capability logic does, but only if every host hands it the same input bytes, and on v0.15.0 they do not always. In the October 23 weekly demo, catalog core.authorize@1.2.0 returned the same decision, reason, obligations and trace on the browser embedder, the Node embedder and traverse-mcp, but a different policy_hash on traverse-mcp. traverse-mcp re-serializes the request JSON with sorted keys, the embedders pass the caller bytes through, and core.authorize hashes the bytes it receives. With sorted-key input, all three hosts were byte-identical. traverse#1722 tracks one input-bytes contract for every host plus a cross-host conformance fixture; it is open.',
